2. **The bot**: Optionally you can have a bot that comes along with your app. The bot is a user that represents your app in every workspace that your app is installed.
You can use the bot to display useful information about your app logic or simply use it to communicate with users. For every workspace you will have a different bot ID.
When your app is installed in a workspace the bot user will be created and your app will receive an authorization code that, when used, will generate access tokens for both the user who installed your app and the bot. See [Authorization](https://cake-com.github.io/pumble-node-sdk/authorization.html).

Your app can use the Pumble API on behalf of every user that has authorized it, or the bot in the workspace where your app is installed. In order to use the built-in ApiClient you need to set up the `tokenStore` in your App and enable `redirect` to be able to capture user [authorizations](https://cake-com.github.io/pumble-node-sdk/authorization.html).
typescript
```
const app: App = {
tokenStore: new JsonFileTokenStore('tokens.json'),
redirect: { enable: true }
//... Triggers
};
```

